</div></header>
<main>
<div id="searchResults"></div>
<section class="hero"><h2>Methods &amp; sources</h2><p>Every figure on this site is compiled by the National Statistics Office of Caldoria from a named survey or register, checked before publication, and revised openly when better data arrive.</p></section>
<div class="card"><h3>Where each figure comes from</h3>
<table class="sortable"><thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Source</th><th>How it is collected</th><th>Latest</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Population</td><td>Population Estimates</td><td>Civil register plus annual household survey of 24,000 homes</td><td>Mid-2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Economy</td><td>National Accounts</td><td>Business survey of 8,500 firms plus tax and customs records</td><td>Q3 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Labour</td><td>Labour Force Survey</td><td>Quarterly survey of 18,000 households, ages 15–74</td><td>Q3 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Prices</td><td>Consumer Prices</td><td>612 items priced monthly in 42 towns</td><td>Oct 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Regions</td><td>Regional GDP</td><td>Regional business survey plus administrative records</td><td>2025 final</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wages</td><td>Earnings Survey</td><td>Annual survey of 6,200 employers</td><td>2026</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<div class="grid2">
<div class="card"><h3>How figures are checked</h3><p>1. <strong>Collection:</strong> trained interviewers and audited business returns; missing answers are followed up, not guessed.</p><p>2. <strong>Validation:</strong> every series is checked against the previous period, the same period last year, and independent registers. A move larger than 3 standard deviations is investigated before publication.</p><p>3. <strong>Seasonal adjustment:</strong> GDP, unemployment and prices are published both raw and seasonally adjusted; this site shows the adjusted series.</p><p>4. <strong>Revision:</strong> quarterly figures are revised twice as late data arrive. Revisions are published with the old and new values side by side.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Definitions</h3><p><strong>Unemployment rate:</strong> unemployed people as a share of the labour force (employed + unemployed), ages 15–74.</p><p><strong>GDP:</strong> the value of all goods and services produced in Caldoria, in current prices unless “real” is stated.</p><p><strong>CPI inflation:</strong> the change in the consumer prices index over 12 months.</p><p><strong>Median wage:</strong> the wage at the middle of the distribution — half of full-time workers earn more, half earn less.</p><p><strong>Caldor (CLD):</strong> Caldoria's currency. 1 CLD = 100 senti.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="card"><h3>Release calendar</h3>
<table><thead><tr><th>Release</th><th>Next date</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Consumer Prices, November 2026</td><td>17 December 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Labour Force Survey, Q4 2026</td><td>21 January 2027</td></tr>
<tr><td>National Accounts, Q4 2026</td><td>11 February 2027</td></tr>
<tr><td>Population Estimates, end-2026</td><td>04 March 2027</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p class="source">Contact: statistics@caldoria.example — the NSO answers questions about any figure on this site. Caldoria is a fictional country; its statistics are invented for this site and are internally consistent.</p></div>
<p><a class="btn" href="index.html">← Back home</a></p>
</main>
